From 598870cba9ce739f457d581124acad50864ec380 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:00:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Offer video when placing a Teams video call

The Phone app dials a video call with {"address", "video": true}, but
the call went out voice only: our offer had no video m-line and the
invitation named ["Audio"] alone.

For a video call, when the engine has video, offer a bundled H264
m-line sendrecv with our video SSRC and invite with ["Audio",
"Video"]. The far side's answer then decides the camera: its
direction, mirrored, says whether we send, and its fmtp how large. The
video m-line is now built by one function for our answers and offers.

Answering a call, name "Video" in the acceptance and renegotiation
answers too when that answer sends our video. With ["Audio"] the
Teams Android app offered its own video sendonly and never took ours.
A voice call is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
